          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %li
                %a{:href => "#examples"} Examples
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
            is
            %strong
              locally
              = succeed "-connected" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            if it has properties that ensure that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
            over it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} locally ∞-connected (∞,1)-topos
          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Call an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %strong locally contractible
              if every constant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaf"} (∞,1)-presheaf
              on it is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf"} (∞,1)-sheaf
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            More explicitly, this means that every covering sieve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            on an object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\in C
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(R)
            (which is just itself, if it is incarnated as a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicategory"} quasicategory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan-Quillen+model+structure"} Kan-Quillen model structure
            on simplicial sets. For the sheaf condition for a constant presheaf on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Gpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in \infty Gpd
            is that the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Const
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mi R
                  %mi Const
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Const(X)(U) = X \to \lim_R Const(X)
            is an equivalence, but
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mi R
                    %mi Const
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Map
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_R Const(X) = Map(N(R),X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(R)
            is contractible as an
            = succeed "-groupoid." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %h2#properties Properties
          .num_defn
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              By the general notion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-colimit
              the constant
              = succeed "-presheaf" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} adjoint (∞,1)-functor
              given by taking colimits
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %mo ↪
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi L
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ←
                        %mi Const
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %munder
                            %mi lim
                            %mo →
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sh_{(\infty,1)}(C)
                    \\underoverset{\hookrightarrow}{\overset{L}{\longleftarrow}}{\bot}
                    PSh_{(\infty,1)}(C)
                    \\stackrel{
                    \\overset{\lim_\to}{\longrightarrow}
                    }
                    {
                    \\underset{Const}{\leftarrow}
                    }
                    \\infty Grpd
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
              sits by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} full and faithful (∞,1)-functor
              inside presheaves and by assumption that every constant
              = succeed "-presheaf" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "-sheaf," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} equivalences
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Sh
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi L
                            %mi Const
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi PSh
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Const
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mn ∞
                            %mi Grpd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mo →
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    Sh(X, L Const S)
                    \&amp;\simeq
                    PSh(X, Const S)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\infty Grpd(\lim_\to X , S)
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          %h2#examples Examples
          .num_defn
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be an 1-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              such that every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+hypercover"} split hypercover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to U
              such that contracting all representables to points yields a weak equivalence. Equivalently, if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_\to : [C^{op}, sSet] \to sSet
              sends this to a weak equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mi Y
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo =
                    %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\lim_\to Y \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} \lim_\to U = *
                    \\,
            %p
              Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is locally
              = succeed "-connected." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We may
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} present
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(\infty,1)}(C)
              by the projective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op}, sSet]_{proj}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localized
              at the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
              projections
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\coprod_i U_i) \to U
              for each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
              family
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to U\}
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p
              It is immediate that we have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi const
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\underset{\rightarrow}{\lim} \dashv const)
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} global model structure on simplicial presheaves
              on both sides. Now by the
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/simplicial+Quillen+adjunction#Recognition"} recognition theorem for simplicial Quillen adjunctions
              for this to descend to a Quillen adjunction on the local model structure it is sufficient that the left adjoint preserves the cofibrations of the local model structure and (already) that the right adjoint preserves the fibration objects. Since left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization of model categories
              does not change the cofibrations, the first of these is immediate.
            %p
              This means that to establish the claim it is now sufficient to show that constant simplicial presheaves already satisfy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
              for a locally
              = succeed "-connected" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %p
              By the discussion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+resolution"} cofibrant resolution
              at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
              we have that a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+hypercover"} split hypercover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to U
              is a cofibrant
